window.__LDNDRC_PAGES = Object.assign(window.__LDNDRC_PAGES || {}, {"gazebo-gzweb":"<p>The simulator is split in two: physics runs headless inside the <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"pod\" tabindex=\"0\">pod</span>, and only the scene is sent to the browser.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-pieces\">The pieces</h2><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Piece</th>\n<th>Where</th>\n<th>Port</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>gz sim</code> (<span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gazebo\" tabindex=\"0\">Gazebo</span> Harmonic)</td>\n<td><span class=\"term\" data-term=\"session\" tabindex=\"0\">session</span> <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"pod\" tabindex=\"0\">pod</span></td>\n<td>headless</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>gazebo-web</code> bridge</td>\n<td><span class=\"term\" data-term=\"session\" tabindex=\"0\">session</span> <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"pod\" tabindex=\"0\">pod</span></td>\n<td><code>9002</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gzweb\" tabindex=\"0\">gzweb</span> viewer (Three.js)</td>\n<td>browser</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>turtlebot3-sim</code> launcher</td>\n<td>editor terminal</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><code>gazebo-web</code> is supervised, so it restarts on its own. <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gazebo\" tabindex=\"0\">Gazebo</span> is <strong>not</strong> supervised — the student launches it in the foreground so they can see its logs and choose a world.</p>\n<h2 id=\"starting-a-world\">Starting a world</h2><p>From the editor terminal:</p>\n<div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">bash</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">turtlebot3-sim              <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># obstacle world, burger model</span>\nturtlebot3-sim empty        <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># empty world</span>\nturtlebot3-sim house        <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># house world</span>\nTURTLEBOT3_MODEL=waffle_pi turtlebot3-sim house</code></pre></div><p>Then open the <code>gazebo</code> tab. The scene streams in over the <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"websocket\" tabindex=\"0\">websocket</span>. Drive it from a second terminal:</p>\n<div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">bash</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">turtlebot3-teleop.sh</code></pre></div><h2 id=\"the-rule-that-causes-most-blank-screens\">The rule that causes most blank screens</h2><p><strong>One <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gazebo\" tabindex=\"0\">Gazebo</span> server per workspace.</strong> A second <code>gz sim</code> creates a duplicate world and robot, and the viewer cannot tell which one to draw. Stop the first with <code>Ctrl-C</code>, or use:</p>\n<div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">bash</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">turtlebot3-sim --force house</code></pre></div><h2 id=\"why-the-scene-is-blank\">Why the scene is blank</h2><p>A blank viewer is almost always one of three things, in this order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>no <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gazebo\" tabindex=\"0\">Gazebo</span> server running (nothing to broadcast)</li>\n<li>the world lacks the <code>SceneBroadcaster</code> plugin</li>\n<li>the bridge on <code>:9002</code> is down or not proxied</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">bash</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">supervisorctl status\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">tail</span> -50 /tmp/gazebo-web.err.log</code></pre></div><h2 id=\"custom-worlds\">Custom worlds</h2><div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">bash</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">gz sim -s -v 3 ~/dev_ws/src/my_workshop/worlds/maze.sdf -r</code></pre></div><p>The <code>SceneBroadcaster</code> plugin is mandatory. Without it <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gazebo\" tabindex=\"0\">Gazebo</span> renders locally and publishes nothing.</p>\n<h2 id=\"desktop-fallback\">Desktop fallback</h2><p>If a student needs <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gazebo\" tabindex=\"0\">Gazebo</span>&#39;s GUI, set <code>TURTLEBOT3_GAZEBO_GUI=true</code> and use the Selkies desktop tab. It is slower, but it is the escape hatch when a custom plugin does not stream.</p>\n<h2 id=\"check-it-yourself\">Check it yourself</h2><div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">bash</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">kubectl -n ldndrc <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">exec</span> &lt;session-pod&gt; -- supervisorctl status\ncurl -s -o /dev/null -w <span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;%{http_code}\\n&#x27;</span> -H <span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;Host: gazebo.ros-platform.local&#x27;</span> http://127.0.0.1:8082/</code></pre></div>","code-server":"<p><code>code-server</code> is VS Code compiled to run on a server and render in a browser. For most students it is the actual product: the editor, the integrated terminal, and the place every command in these docs is typed.</p>\n<p>It runs inside the <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"session\" tabindex=\"0\">session</span> <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"pod\" tabindex=\"0\">pod</span> on port <code>7682</code>, behind the <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gateway\" tabindex=\"0\">gateway</span> at <code>editor.ros-platform.local</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-not-a-local-editor\">Why not a local editor?</h2><p>Because the code has to run where ROS and <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gazebo\" tabindex=\"0\">Gazebo</span> run. A local editor would need a tunnel, a matching toolchain, and a way to ship files back and forth. The editor living next to the robot removes all three problems.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-trade-off\">The trade-off</h2><p>The browser editor is limited by the browser: no native extensions that need a GUI, no local filesystem, keyboard shortcuts that fight the <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"host\" tabindex=\"0\">host</span> OS. For <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"ros2\" tabindex=\"0\">ROS 2</span> Python and launch files it is more than enough. For heavy C++ debugging, the <a href=\"#/selkies\" class=\"topic-link\">The streamed desktop</a> desktop exists.</p>\n<h2 id=\"check-it-yourself\">Check it yourself</h2><div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">bash</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">curl -s -o /dev/null -w <span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;%{http_code}\\n&#x27;</span> \\\n  -H <span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;Host: editor.ros-platform.local&#x27;</span> -H <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;Cookie: <span class=\"hljs-variable\">$COOKIE</span>&quot;</span> \\\n  http://127.0.0.1:8082/\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\"># 200</span></code></pre></div>","selkies":"<p>Selkies streams a real Linux desktop to the browser over WebRTC. It exists because some tools will never work in a browser pane: RViz, rqt, <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gazebo\" tabindex=\"0\">Gazebo</span>&#39;s GUI, anything that needs a window manager and a GPU-accelerated surface.</p>\n<p>It runs on port <code>8080</code> inside the <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"session\" tabindex=\"0\">session</span> <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"pod\" tabindex=\"0\">pod</span> and is reachable at <code>desktop.ros-platform.local</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"when-to-use-it\">When to use it</h2><ul>\n<li>Visualising TF trees in RViz.</li>\n<li>Running <code>rqt</code> plugins.</li>\n<li>Debugging a <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gazebo\" tabindex=\"0\">Gazebo</span> world that will not stream through the browser viewer.</li>\n<li>Anything that needs a second window.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-2-0-0-migration\">The 2.0.0 migration</h2><p>Selkies 2.0.0 changed its signalling and container layout. The migration checkpoint verified the desktop returns <code>200</code> through the <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gateway\" tabindex=\"0\">gateway</span> and that input works end to end. It is the reason the <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"workspace-image\" tabindex=\"0\">workspace image</span> pins a specific Selkies version rather than tracking latest.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-cost\">The cost</h2><p>WebRTC is bandwidth-hungry and latency-sensitive. On a congested workshop Wi-Fi, the editor stays usable while the desktop degrades. That is why it is an escape hatch, not the default tool — see <a href=\"#/uiux-principles\" class=\"topic-link\">Focus over window management</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"check-it-yourself\">Check it yourself</h2><div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">bash</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">curl -s -o /dev/null -w <span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;%{http_code}\\n&#x27;</span> \\\n  -H <span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;Host: desktop.ros-platform.local&#x27;</span> -H <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;Cookie: <span class=\"hljs-variable\">$COOKIE</span>&quot;</span> \\\n  http://127.0.0.1:8082/</code></pre></div>","workspace-image":"<p>The <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"session\" tabindex=\"0\">session</span> image is where ROS, <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gazebo\" tabindex=\"0\">Gazebo</span>, the editor, the desktop, and the scene bridge all meet. Building it is a chain, not a single <code>docker build</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-chain\">The chain</h2><ol>\n<li><strong>Base layers</strong> — Ubuntu, NVIDIA runtime hooks, common tooling.</li>\n<li><strong><span class=\"term\" data-term=\"ros2\" tabindex=\"0\">ROS 2</span> Jazzy + <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gazebo\" tabindex=\"0\">Gazebo</span> Harmonic</strong> — the robotics payload.</li>\n<li><strong>Workspace layer</strong> — <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"code-server\" tabindex=\"0\">code-server</span>, Selkies, <code>gazebo-web</code>, supervisor config, <code>turtlebot3</code> packages and worlds.</li>\n<li><strong>Immutable tag</strong> — a content hash, never <code>latest</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"why-the-tag-is-a-hash\">Why the tag is a hash</h2><p>The image is imported into each <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"host\" tabindex=\"0\">Host</span>&#39;s <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"containerd\" tabindex=\"0\">containerd</span>. If two <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"host\" tabindex=\"0\">Hosts</span> have different images under the same tag, two students in the same class get different robots and nobody can reproduce the bug. An immutable sha tag makes that impossible to do by accident.</p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-it-onto-a-laptop\">Getting it onto a laptop</h2><div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">bash</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">docker save ldndrc/ros2-gz:&lt;sha&gt; -o workspace.tar\nk3d image import workspace.tar -c ldndrc     <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># demo</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\"># real cluster: push to a local registry the Hosts can pull from</span></code></pre></div><p>The budget for all of this is <a href=\"#/disk-budget\" class=\"topic-link\">The disk budget</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"check-it-yourself\">Check it yourself</h2><div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">bash</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">kubectl -n ldndrc get deploy \\\n  -o jsonpath=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;{.items[*].spec.template.spec.containers[*].image}&#x27;</span></code></pre></div>","disk-budget":"<p>The <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"workspace-image\" tabindex=\"0\">workspace image</span> is roughly 10 GB. That is not a build problem — it is a planning problem, because every <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"host\" tabindex=\"0\">Host</span> has to hold it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-numbers-that-matter\">The numbers that matter</h2><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Budget</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Image, compressed</td>\n<td>~4–5 GB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Image, on disk per <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"node\" tabindex=\"0\">node</span></td>\n<td>~10 GB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Free disk required</td>\n<td>~25 GB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Student home <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"pvc\" tabindex=\"0\">PVC</span></td>\n<td><code>5Gi</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Multiply by the number of <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"host\" tabindex=\"0\">Hosts</span>. A five-laptop workshop is asking for 50 GB of image storage before a single student has saved a file.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-the-compression-work-bought\">What the compression work bought</h2><p>The compression checkpoint recorded what each layer costs and which ones can be squashed or reordered. The result was a smaller image and a documented number, so &quot;it fits on a workshop laptop&quot; became a measurement rather than a hope.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-failure-mode\">The failure mode</h2><p><code>ImagePullBackOff</code> on a <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"session\" tabindex=\"0\">session</span> <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"pod\" tabindex=\"0\">pod</span> usually means the image is missing on the <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"node\" tabindex=\"0\">node</span> that got scheduled — not that the registry is down. On the demo, re-run <code>k3d image import</code>. On a real cluster, check the local registry and the <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"node\" tabindex=\"0\">node</span>&#39;s disk.</p>\n<h2 id=\"check-it-yourself\">Check it yourself</h2><div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">bash</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">docker images | grep ldndrc\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">df</span> -h /var/lib/rancher</code></pre></div>"});
